 # Radiance-field optimization
 
-Also called: Differentiable radiance field optimization, Inverse radiance field rendering
 
 ## Overview
-Radiance-field optimization is the family of inverse rendering methods that reconstruct a 3D scene representation by minimizing the photometric error between rendered images and ground-truth observations [S2]. It solves the problem of novel view synthesis by training a neural network to directly learn color and opacity (or density) values using the discrete volume rendering equation [S2]. Unlike explicit mesh-based reconstruction, radiance-field optimization relies on the differentiability of the forward volume rendering operator to propagate gradients from pixel space to the scene representation [G].
